# Shell scripts must check out with LF endings on every machine.
#
# HazeHub is developed on Windows, where git is usually set to convert to CRLF
# on checkout. A .sh file with CRLF endings fails on macOS and Linux with
# "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M", which is a confusing way to discover
# a line-ending problem. This pins them regardless of anyone's local config.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The PowerShell counterparts are Windows-only, so they keep CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
